# Cross-machine

Resolve devices with `resolve_device`. Allowed preferences: `auto`, `cuda`, `mps`, `cpu`. An explicit preference must not fall back to another device.

`auto` is for smoke and for `scripts/env_check.py`. Confirmatory CUDA configs set `device: cuda` so a Mac clone fails instead of silently running MPS under a CUDA label.

Every run header stores device name, capability, torch version, and platform. `assert_same_machine` before pooling.

Canonical CUDA results come from the CUDA machine named in `docs/STATE.md`. MPS results are reported as MPS. Do not claim bit-exact agreement across devices.

Torch wheels: cu132 index on Windows and Linux, PyPI on macOS. See ADR-003.
